Error [jet.RejectOutsideTemplate]: `reject` runs only inside a marker's `expand` template.
  --> tests/ui/marker_declarations/reject_outside_a_marker_template.jet:11:5
    |
 11 |     reject(Oops{})
    |     ^^^^^^
 Why: `reject(value)` raises a diagnostic at a marker's use site while the compiler expands the marker; ordinary code has no use site to report at, so the call has nothing to run.
 Fix: Move the check into a marker's `expand: fn(self, target: Target)` body, or return an error value from this function instead.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0962
